-- title:
--   Galois-fixed basis of a stable Riemann–Roch space on X_H(M)
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ be a nonzero natural number, $H$ a subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$, and let $F =$ `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` be the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ generated by the image of the $q$-expansion function field `xHFunctionField M H` of level $\Gamma_H(M)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ under the coefficientwise embedding $\mathbb{Q}((q)) \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$. Let $S$ be any set of $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra automorphisms of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and let $E$ be a divisor of $F/\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, that is, a finitely supported $\mathbb{Z}$-valued function on the places of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (valuation subrings of $F$ containing $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, distinct from $F$ itself, and principal ideal rings). Assume that for every $\sigma \in S$ the divisor $E$ is fixed by the action of $\sigma$ obtained from `arithmeticGalois`, the homomorphism sending $\sigma$ to the semilinear automorphism of $F$ given by applying $\sigma$ to the Laurent coefficients, paired with $\sigma$ on $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Assume further that the Riemann–Roch space $\{f \in F : v(f) \le \exp(E(v)) \text{ for all places } v\}$ of $E$ is finite-dimensional over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, of dimension $n$. Then there is a family $b : \mathrm{Fin}\,n \to F$ with all $b_i$ in the Riemann–Roch space of $E$, linearly independent over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and such that $\sigma \cdot b_i = b_i$ for all $i$ and all $\sigma \in S$. The conclusion is phrased as a linearly independent family of cardinality equal to the dimension lying in the space, rather than literally as a basis of it.
--
--   This is Galois descent for the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-vector space $L(E)$: a Riemann–Roch space on the modular curve $X_H(M)$ whose divisor is stable under a set of arithmetic (coefficientwise) Galois automorphisms admits a spanning family of Galois-fixed functions, obtained from [`Module.exists_basis_forall_semilinear_apply_eq_of_isGalois`](thm.html#Module.exists_basis_forall_semilinear_apply_eq_of_isGalois). It is used in the construction of prolongation data at places of $X_H(M)$, where a basis of $L(E)$ defined over $\mathbb{Q}$ is required.
-- source:
